Subject: [PATCH] pqc: initialize the PQC subsystem eagerly in the postmaster

pqc_preflight_check() (called from PostmasterMain) logged
"liboqs available: no" because pqc_init() was only ever called
lazily from the KEM/SIG paths on first use. liboqs was linked and
fully functional; the status flag was simply read before init ran,
and every backend re-initialized independently. Initialize once in
the postmaster so the status is accurate and forked backends inherit
the initialized state.

---
--- a/src/backend/crypto/pqc/pqc_preflight.c
+++ b/src/backend/crypto/pqc/pqc_preflight.c
@@ -137,6 +137,14 @@
 	}
 #endif
 
+	/*
+	 * Eagerly initialize the PQC subsystem here in the postmaster so the
+	 * status logged below is accurate, and so every forked backend inherits
+	 * an initialized liboqs state instead of lazily re-initializing on first
+	 * PQC use.
+	 */
+	(void) pqc_init();
+
 	/* Log PQC subsystem status */
 	elog(LOG, "FortressQL: PQC subsystem initialized (liboqs available: %s)",
 		 pqc_is_available() ? "yes" : "no");
